// @title   TropeLang Concept Library — CamelCase aliases
// @version 0.1
// @note    Bridges the CamelCase spelling of a concept (as it appears in `imply` components) to its
//          canonical lowercase declaration (S13). `imply DecadentCourt -> [Corruption, …]` references
//          `concept corruption`; these aliases let the CamelCase form resolve without rewriting every
//          trope. The CANONICAL form is the lowercase concept — prefer it in new code; CamelCase here is
//          a legacy-compatibility bridge, not a second symbol (casing is otherwise meaning-bearing).
//
// Import: import "trl/concepts/concept_aliases.trl"

alias Atonement     -> atonement
alias Audience      -> audience
alias Author        -> author
alias Bargaining    -> bargaining
alias Beginning     -> beginning
alias Comedy        -> comedy
alias Corruption    -> corruption
alias Cost          -> cost
alias Cruelty       -> cruelty
alias Deception     -> deception
alias Denial        -> denial
alias Despair       -> despair
alias Dignity       -> dignity
alias Empathy       -> empathy
alias Ending        -> ending
alias Fate          -> fate
alias Guilt         -> guilt
alias Honor         -> honor
alias Kishotenketsu -> kishotenketsu
alias Love          -> love
alias Loyalty       -> loyalty
alias Recognition   -> recognition
alias Revelation    -> revelation
alias Suffering     -> suffering
alias Temptation    -> temptation
alias Tragedy       -> tragedy
